WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.339
- Skin's very dry.

00:00:01.339 --> 00:00:02.570
- I know.

00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:03.403
- Did you moisturize it?
- Yes.

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:04.530
- Okay.
- It's very bumpy.

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:05.620
Hi, I'm Garrett.

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:06.453
- And I'm Niki.

00:00:06.453 --> 00:00:08.390
- We're fascinated by
how other people live.

00:00:08.390 --> 00:00:09.223
- [Niki] So we're gonna try and find some

00:00:09.223 --> 00:00:10.510
really interesting living situations.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:11.430
- [Garrett] And live there,

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:13.100
experiencing a totally
different lifestyle.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:14.840
- [Niki] To see which ones
bring us closer together,

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:16.170
- [Garrett] Or push us further apart.

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:18.368
- This week, we're living in an RV.

00:00:18.368 --> 00:00:20.050
- Why'd you emphasize it like that?

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:21.210
- I don't know.

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:22.110
- I drove it here.

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:36.330
- Hi, my name is David, and this is my RV.

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:40.370
It's a 32 foot, fits six
people very, very comfortably.

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:42.830
I've never had anybody take my RV out

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:44.600
and say, "We didn't have a good time."

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:47.178
It's usually an experience
that they didn't expect

00:00:47.178 --> 00:00:49.780
and plan on doing so again in the future

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:51.430
because they had such a fun time.

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:52.263
- Hi.

00:00:52.263 --> 00:00:53.625
- I'm David.

00:00:53.625 --> 00:00:54.458
- I'm Niki, nice to meet you.

00:00:54.458 --> 00:00:55.291
- You guys wanna take a look?

00:00:55.291 --> 00:00:56.631
- Yeah please, let's do it.

00:00:56.631 --> 00:00:57.638
- Come on in.

00:00:57.638 --> 00:00:58.471
- We're spending three days in an RV

00:00:58.471 --> 00:00:59.304
driving around Arizona.

00:00:59.304 --> 00:01:00.642
- When you think of RV,

00:01:00.642 --> 00:01:02.240
I think the destination you
think of is the Grand Canyon.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:04.600
I think it's gonna be a perfect trip.

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:05.433
- If we're going somewhere,

00:01:05.433 --> 00:01:07.550
I wanna get there efficiently and quickly.

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:09.240
RVs are all about taking your time,

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:10.235
taking the scenic route.

00:01:10.235 --> 00:01:12.410
If we wanna go see the Grand Canyon,

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:13.320
let's just go see the Grand Canyon

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:14.510
and then fly the hell out of there.

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:15.610
- People live in these things.

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:19.606
My grandparents spent
months at a time in an RV.

00:01:19.606 --> 00:01:21.730
- (sighs) I don't get it,

00:01:21.730 --> 00:01:25.510
it's not efficient, inconvenient,

00:01:25.510 --> 00:01:26.600
slow (laughs).

00:01:28.596 --> 00:01:29.740
Oh, okay.

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:31.389
- What'd you think it was gonna be?

00:01:31.389 --> 00:01:32.370
- [Niki] I don't know.

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:33.330
- Wow, look at this TV.

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:34.870
- Oh, there's a TV.

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:37.304
- And I fit, just right.
- Yeah, kind of.

00:01:37.304 --> 00:01:39.410
- I think this is really
gonna put Garrett's size

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:41.956
to the test because
there's no space in this.

00:01:41.956 --> 00:01:45.500
- I'm 6'7, people, we
gotta start living bigger.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:47.776
I know everybody's trying to
downsize and stuff, stop it.

00:01:47.776 --> 00:01:49.715
- Now, this is the slide.

00:01:49.715 --> 00:01:51.911
We're gonna extend it right now.

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:52.744
- What?

00:01:54.791 --> 00:01:56.458
- [Niki] Oh, no way.

00:01:57.559 --> 00:01:58.910
This house is getting bigger.

00:01:58.910 --> 00:01:59.810
- [Garrett] That's amazing.

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:02.850
- Obviously, there's not a
lot of room inside of it.

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:04.300
- There's only one actual bed,

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:06.280
but then I think a bunch of other places

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:08.070
fold out into beds, which is neat,

00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:09.720
a lot of things that have dual purposes.

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:10.900
- You can eat over here.

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:12.690
This also turns into a bed.

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:14.270
This'll probably be where you're sleeping.

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:15.430
I did measure it.

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:16.930
It's eight feet across so you'll have

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:18.260
plenty of room up there.

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:21.100
- Yeah, oh my gosh, it's super long.

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:22.640
- [Niki] Wow, we were
so worried about you.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:24.269
- It has a shower, bathroom.

00:02:24.269 --> 00:02:26.480
I measured it, it is actually 6'10.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:28.509
- [Garrett] Oh really, wow,
well that's gonna be great.

00:02:28.509 --> 00:02:30.990
- [David] Come in here, I
wanna show you guys something.

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:32.930
Right here (toilet flushes)

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:34.376
- [Niki] That's it?

00:02:34.376 --> 00:02:35.230
I can do that.

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:36.900
Have you had any toilet disasters?

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:37.960
- I have not.

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:38.933
- Has anyone else?

00:02:38.933 --> 00:02:40.502
- They have not.

00:02:40.502 --> 00:02:42.450
The kitchen is complete,

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:45.330
it's everything that you would
expect inside your kitchen.

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:47.831
You got a refrigerator and freezer here.

00:02:47.831 --> 00:02:49.350
- [Niki] This is like a kitchen.

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:50.790
- It is absolutely a kitchen.

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:52.190
- What'd you think it was gonna be?

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:53.570
- We are in a car.

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:55.280
And it's safe to cook in here?

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:56.550
- Absolutely.

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:59.197
- When you move, everything
needs to be fastened down

00:02:59.197 --> 00:03:00.490
and latched away.
- Pretty much, pretty much.

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:02.590
You're gonna hear some
rattles on the road.

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:03.976
It's okay.

00:03:03.976 --> 00:03:06.327
- So I don't know how the RV works.

00:03:06.327 --> 00:03:09.020
It's got a water tank,
it's got electricity.

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:10.990
Do we need to charge it like a Tesla?

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:12.720
- The only context I have for RVs

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:13.890
are what I've seen in movies.

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:16.155
Just really worried about
a poop situation happening.

00:03:16.155 --> 00:03:18.270
- Okay, fun part.

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:19.370
- [Niki] Is that the poop hole?

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:20.819
- [Garrett] Niki.

00:03:20.819 --> 00:03:22.040
- I wanna make sure we get that down.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:24.690
- You're gonna have sewer
and electricity and water.

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:25.523
The alligator clip.

00:03:25.523 --> 00:03:27.336
- [Garrett] There's the
alligator, the matches.

00:03:27.336 --> 00:03:28.570
- Put it back on.

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:30.860
Normally, when you pull
up and you'll have a hole

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:32.120
in the ground and stuff like that,

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:33.582
you'll see a rock next to it,

00:03:33.582 --> 00:03:35.780
which is there for a reason, all right?

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:37.464
You put this in the hole and then

00:03:37.464 --> 00:03:39.050
you just kind of put a rock on top.

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:40.584
- That's not gonna move around.

00:03:40.584 --> 00:03:41.720
- What if you don't put the rock on top?

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:42.820
- Don't, don't.

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:44.116
- [David] Nothing.

00:03:44.116 --> 00:03:45.940
- That's not what happened
in the Ice Cube movie.

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:47.540
- Given where our relationship is now,

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:49.250
I think spending all this
time together in an RV

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:50.850
will actually push us together.

00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:52.820
It is such an obstacle thing,

00:03:52.820 --> 00:03:54.618
we have to really work together

00:03:54.618 --> 00:03:57.730
to accomplish living
in this motor vehicle.

00:03:57.730 --> 00:04:00.560
- With this living situation,
there are too many obstacles.

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:02.100
I think we're gonna be
at each other's throats.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:03.417
- All right.
- Let's go.

00:04:03.417 --> 00:04:07.010
- I'm going back here.

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:09.120
- We basically have to
fasten everything down

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:11.090
while we're driving.
- Oh god.

00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:12.760
- You already falling over?

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:14.800
You're just gonna sleep the
whole time I drive, aren't you?

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:15.633
- Yeah.

00:04:15.633 --> 00:04:18.070
I'm not a bad driver,
but this thing is so big.

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:18.930
Garrett can drive it.

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:20.640
This is his sized vehicle.

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:21.861
You sure you can drive this thing?

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:23.099
- We're gonna find out.

00:04:23.099 --> 00:04:25.752
- We're on our way to the Grand Canyon.

00:04:25.752 --> 00:04:29.673
On a scale of one to ten,
how scared are you right now?

00:04:29.673 --> 00:04:30.760
- Like an eight.

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:32.330
I don't know how I'm gonna make this turn,

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:34.440
I don't know how I'm gonna make, I don't,

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.771
you gotta, I can't see the mirror.

00:04:35.771 --> 00:04:36.604
- Oh my god, okay.

00:04:36.604 --> 00:04:38.310
- The drive wasn't so bad.

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:40.071
It's a lot of vehicle.

00:04:40.071 --> 00:04:41.896
- You won't hit that car.

00:04:41.896 --> 00:04:43.000
- I think I will.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:43.950
- I don't think so.

00:04:44.821 --> 00:04:47.017
- Look at you, driving a bus.

00:04:47.017 --> 00:04:48.740
- Yes, look at me.

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:51.252
- This is finally a you-sized vehicle.

00:04:51.252 --> 00:04:53.780
- Wow, does this feel dangerous.

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:55.515
- [Niki] You're doing a great job.

00:04:55.515 --> 00:04:56.810
Keep your eyes on the road.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:59.760
I'm already tired.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:01.630
I'm gonna go take a nap in the back.

00:05:02.978 --> 00:05:03.811
Ah.

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:07.313
- Am I allowed to be back
here while you're driving?

00:05:07.313 --> 00:05:10.460
The people in the car behind
us can definitely see me.

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:11.820
While Garrett was driving this afternoon,

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:13.130
I laid down back here,

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:15.070
but it's a really bumpy ride

00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:16.890
so everything just felt super crazy

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:17.950
and everything was shaking.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:19.550
- [Garrett] I actually was really happy

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:21.500
that Niki was able to lay down and nap

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:23.790
while I was driving, and be comfortable

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:25.290
because then it doesn't feel as cramped.

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:27.390
It doesn't feel as sort of arduous

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:29.060
as a road trip can feel.

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:30.950
At first, I was very
nervous driving this thing,

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:33.330
but then, after just 10 miles,

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:35.280
I was very comfortable doing it.

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:38.347
- We made it, Garrett drove
us to the Grand Canyon.

00:05:38.347 --> 00:05:40.900
- Couldn't have done it without
you asleep in the back, Nik.

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:41.906
- It was so bumpy.

00:05:41.906 --> 00:05:44.080
It's very dark and I have
no idea where we are.

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:46.731
But now we gotta go hook up the poop hose

00:05:46.731 --> 00:05:49.050
so Garrett can poop.

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:50.690
I don't think Garrett's
used the bathroom yet.

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:51.920
I think he's scared.

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:53.100
Welcome to my crib.

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:57.240
There's water, that's for the poop.

00:05:57.240 --> 00:05:58.854
- There's that rock he was talking about.

00:05:58.854 --> 00:06:00.410
- What do we do first?

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:03.017
- Water and power.

00:06:03.017 --> 00:06:04.517
- Water and power.

00:06:05.591 --> 00:06:08.091
That's where we put the power.

00:06:10.420 --> 00:06:12.710
- Which one's 30?

00:06:12.710 --> 00:06:14.810
- [Niki] There were a few learning hiccups

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:19.407
about how to hook up this
machine, transformer, bus.

00:06:19.407 --> 00:06:21.360
- This is hard.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:24.290
It goes in both ways and
doesn't turn either way.

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:27.720
Let's do the water.

00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:32.010
Hooking it up to the
system was a little weird.

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:33.460
All right, it's accepting it.

00:06:36.399 --> 00:06:38.100
- We have water.

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:40.345
- It seems to be leaking pretty,

00:06:40.345 --> 00:06:41.390
- [Niki] Do we just leave it?

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:44.410
- [Garrett] Maybe shut
it off for a second.

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:47.020
We had a couple hiccups but
I think that was just because

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:48.090
we'd never done it before.

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:50.290
Now, if we had to hook this thing up

00:06:50.290 --> 00:06:52.570
to any place, anywhere in the country,

00:06:52.570 --> 00:06:54.974
I think we'd be able
to do it without issue.

00:06:54.974 --> 00:06:56.202
- There we go.

00:06:56.202 --> 00:06:58.240
We have done it.

00:07:00.124 --> 00:07:00.957
RV.

00:07:02.414 --> 00:07:03.948
(laughs) You missed.

00:07:03.948 --> 00:07:05.260
Garrett and I are really
figuring out each other's quirks,

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:07.727
I think, he eats like a 14-year-old.

00:07:07.727 --> 00:07:10.730
All he wants to eat are cheeseburgers.

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:12.030
All right, well this is going great.

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:13.420
- Yeah, it always goes great for you

00:07:13.420 --> 00:07:14.820
because you just sit and watch me cook.

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:16.320
- There's no space for me to help you.

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:17.560
Do you want me to stand right next to you

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:19.600
and watch burgers brown?

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:20.433
- Yes.

00:07:20.433 --> 00:07:22.160
No, sit down.

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:23.950
Niki and I started getting in

00:07:23.950 --> 00:07:25.440
tiny little fights, a little bit.

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:27.350
- He and I can pick on
each other and it's fine.

00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:29.360
I'll sit back while he makes dinner

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:30.970
and does all the dishes (laughs).

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:32.490
- [Garrett] It does look pretty good, Nik.

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:33.660
You see? (fire alarm beeps)

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:35.020
Oh, shit.

00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:36.390
- [Niki] Just fan it, fan it, don't.

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:39.320
Move, stop, don't, don't.

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:42.420
- Why are you, stop doing it still.

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:43.253
- Ventilation.

00:07:43.253 --> 00:07:45.270
- Okay, well now we found
something for you to do.

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:48.650
It's maybe even a sign
of friendship progress

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:51.330
when you can get in little
fights with your friends

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:53.350
and know that that's gonna be fine.

00:07:53.350 --> 00:07:55.815
Not that that's a good thing. (laughs)

00:07:55.815 --> 00:07:56.810
- [Niki] When I try to
do stuff, he'll be like,

00:07:56.810 --> 00:07:58.050
"No, why would you do it that way,

00:07:58.050 --> 00:08:00.140
I'll do it," he wants to be in control.

00:08:00.140 --> 00:08:01.730
He wants to be in charge, so fine.

00:08:01.730 --> 00:08:03.243
- I'm sick of cooking dinner for her.

00:08:03.243 --> 00:08:06.070
- So tomorrow we'll get up for sunrise?

00:08:06.070 --> 00:08:07.660
- Yeah, tomorrow let's see the sunrise

00:08:07.660 --> 00:08:08.740
over the Grand Canyon.

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:10.059
Okay, goodnight, Niki.

00:08:10.059 --> 00:08:11.059
- Goodnight.

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:22.160
- Well, it's the morning of the first day.

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:25.100
We're going to miss the
sunrise over the Grand Canyon.

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:27.050
I think this was a pretty
optimistic plan to begin with

00:08:27.050 --> 00:08:29.050
'cause I don't think Niki's
ever seen the sunrise.

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:31.710
I'm gonna still try to
get this thing unhooked

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:34.450
so that we can drive around
the Grand Canyon for the day.

00:08:37.288 --> 00:08:40.190
Well, we're all unhooked,

00:08:40.190 --> 00:08:44.650
ready to see the sunrise over
the Grand Canyon. (laughs)

00:08:44.650 --> 00:08:46.250
Looks like it's already pretty risen.

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:47.840
Meanwhile, Niki sleeps.

00:08:49.299 --> 00:08:52.049
(relaxing music)

00:09:03.633 --> 00:09:05.283
Here I am, near the Grand Canyon.

00:09:06.810 --> 00:09:07.643
Wow.

00:09:09.111 --> 00:09:10.990
- So it's about 8:30.

00:09:10.990 --> 00:09:13.120
I think Garrett drove us somewhere

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:14.770
because we were definitely moving.

00:09:14.770 --> 00:09:16.690
I guess he's seeing the
Grand Canyon by himself,

00:09:16.690 --> 00:09:17.740
which is kind of frustrating.

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:21.030
I know that I kind of made it
so that our plan fell through.

00:09:21.030 --> 00:09:22.390
The least he could have
done would have been,

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:25.600
hey, I'm gonna drive us
across the park, is that cool?

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:27.460
There's no water.

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:30.140
So he decided to do all
of this on his own and

00:09:32.145 --> 00:09:34.840
now I'm kind of trapped.

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:35.700
(frustrated grunt)

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:38.760
He's very much used to kind
of doing things on a whim.

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:40.900
It just so happens that him
deciding to do something

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:43.550
by himself also meant
dragging me along in the back

00:09:43.550 --> 00:09:45.240
while I was half asleep.

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:47.050
- So you were awake when we were driving?

00:09:47.050 --> 00:09:48.132
- Of course.

00:09:48.132 --> 00:09:50.327
- And you didn't wanna
ask what we were doing?

00:09:50.327 --> 00:09:51.457
- How?
- I don't know.

00:09:51.457 --> 00:09:53.890
Saying anything, we're all in one room.

00:09:53.890 --> 00:09:55.950
- You could've said, "Hey,
we're gonna go somewhere,

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:56.783
is that cool?"

00:09:56.783 --> 00:09:59.257
- You were asleep, I
didn't wanna wake you up.

00:09:59.257 --> 00:10:01.442
- So you unilaterally decided to do stuff

00:10:01.442 --> 00:10:02.854
without telling me?

00:10:02.854 --> 00:10:05.480
- We made a plan to see the Grand Canyon.

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:06.680
Then she didn't wake up.

00:10:09.230 --> 00:10:12.414
But I'm trying not to become
defensive about things.

00:10:12.414 --> 00:10:13.421
- Fine, let's go.

00:10:13.421 --> 00:10:15.070
- Where's my hat?

00:10:15.070 --> 00:10:16.910
My hair looks terrible.

00:10:16.910 --> 00:10:18.435
Okay.

00:10:18.435 --> 00:10:22.000
Behold, the Grand Canyon parking lot.

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:24.090
So you slept pretty good, were you cold?

00:10:24.090 --> 00:10:25.900
- No, it was fine.

00:10:25.900 --> 00:10:27.350
- Did you use that electric blanket?

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:28.510
- Yeah.

00:10:28.510 --> 00:10:31.440
- It's really gonna be bad
if you don't like this thing.

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:32.418
- Why wouldn't I like it?

00:10:32.418 --> 00:10:33.901
- I don't know.

00:10:33.901 --> 00:10:34.734
Ta da.

00:10:35.698 --> 00:10:37.812
- Oh my god, it's huge.

00:10:37.812 --> 00:10:41.381
- It's pretty big, isn't it?
- Yeah.

00:10:41.381 --> 00:10:42.730
- It's pretty cool.

00:10:42.730 --> 00:10:46.480
I don't know how things
are between us now,

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:48.172
like if we've taken a step back

00:10:48.172 --> 00:10:49.850
or if we're back to where we were.

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:51.570
I don't think we'll know until tomorrow.

00:10:51.570 --> 00:10:53.330
- I was frustrated and I was upset.

00:10:53.330 --> 00:10:55.080
I just need a little bit sometimes

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:57.058
and then I can participate
and then I can be involved

00:10:57.058 --> 00:10:58.910
and I can be invested, but

00:10:58.910 --> 00:11:00.390
Grand Canyon's kind of amazing.

00:11:00.390 --> 00:11:01.750
Wow.

00:11:01.750 --> 00:11:04.477
- That said, there's really
not much to do but look at it.

00:11:04.477 --> 00:11:07.227
(relaxing music)

00:11:15.396 --> 00:11:16.900
(sighs)

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:18.460
- All right, eggs.

00:11:18.460 --> 00:11:21.410
The kitchen is, I'd say,
not the worst kitchen

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:22.790
we've had to live with.

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:24.268
Wait, turn this to gas?

00:11:24.268 --> 00:11:26.496
- Is one lit, is one on gas?

00:11:26.496 --> 00:11:28.363
If one's on gas, turn it off.

00:11:28.363 --> 00:11:29.645
- They're all off.

00:11:29.645 --> 00:11:31.780
I'm starting to understand
a little bit more

00:11:31.780 --> 00:11:34.530
why people enjoy RVs and
there's definitely been parts

00:11:34.530 --> 00:11:35.900
of this experience that I've enjoyed

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:37.780
but a lot of it's still
very challenging for me.

00:11:37.780 --> 00:11:39.940
- Actually, living in this
RV's been a little bit

00:11:39.940 --> 00:11:41.720
rockier than I thought it was going to be.

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:45.110
We'll see tomorrow if it's
really brought us together

00:11:45.110 --> 00:11:47.790
or actually sort of done
damage to our relationship.

00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:49.270
- [Niki] I think I made
the coffee too strong.

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:50.180
- No such thing.

00:11:52.860 --> 00:11:55.970
Whoa, that does smell strong.

00:11:58.873 --> 00:12:01.470
- That's not what it should taste like.

00:12:01.470 --> 00:12:03.210
Next time you decide to drive the van,

00:12:03.210 --> 00:12:04.530
can you tell me first?

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:06.110
- I wanted to let you sleep.

00:12:06.110 --> 00:12:09.187
- Okay, well when you
drive, I don't sleep.

00:12:09.187 --> 00:12:13.737
So just tell me next
time, you can wake me up.

00:12:13.737 --> 00:12:16.002
- [Garrett] Okay, sorry
I didn't wake you up.

00:12:16.002 --> 00:12:17.300
My knees.

00:12:18.240 --> 00:12:19.803
- We should get you a little stool.

00:12:19.803 --> 00:12:21.423
Thanks for doing dishes.

00:12:21.423 --> 00:12:22.640
- Thanks for drying.

00:12:22.640 --> 00:12:24.240
- I don't think either of us knew

00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:26.760
the type of relationship
investment we were getting into

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:28.570
when we decided to live
in this RV together.

00:12:28.570 --> 00:12:31.670
- Over the course of the
day, though, it got better.

00:12:31.670 --> 00:12:33.670
Niki, wanna go for a ride?

00:12:40.003 --> 00:12:40.836
Look at her go.

00:12:43.067 --> 00:12:44.185
Fun?

00:12:44.185 --> 00:12:45.908
- Yeah.

00:12:45.908 --> 00:12:47.500
So I have enough room in
this bathroom to do my hair,

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:50.330
which is nice, quarters are
a little tight still, but

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:52.838
I can at least do this.

00:12:52.838 --> 00:12:54.396
- Okay, I'm gonna go take a shower.

00:12:54.396 --> 00:12:55.400
- Good luck.

00:12:55.400 --> 00:12:57.460
- How am I gonna do this?

00:12:57.460 --> 00:12:59.330
This is taking some planning.

00:13:04.030 --> 00:13:05.580
I forgot to lay out a bath mat.

00:13:07.427 --> 00:13:11.340
- We've gotten really good
at connecting the house up

00:13:11.340 --> 00:13:13.840
to its inputs, which seemed like something

00:13:13.840 --> 00:13:15.314
that we would never get good at.

00:13:15.314 --> 00:13:16.540
- There's still a few buttons and stuff

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:18.290
that I don't know how to work,

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:20.250
so I'm very thankful that
Garrett knows how to use them

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:22.670
and work them, 'cause he's
been kind of taking the reins

00:13:22.670 --> 00:13:25.470
on being in charge of
functioning the vehicle.

00:13:25.470 --> 00:13:28.390
Water, power, TV, RV.

00:13:31.590 --> 00:13:32.423
- High five.

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:35.680
- Shall we transform the area?

00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:37.140
- You wanna transform it into beds?

00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:38.543
- [Niki] Yeah.

00:13:38.543 --> 00:13:39.376
Tomorrow we have a lot of work to do

00:13:39.376 --> 00:13:41.769
to clean up the RV and to pack
up and to get out of here.

00:13:41.769 --> 00:13:44.800
- We are going to refold everything up,

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:48.050
unhook everything, oh,
my nose is bleeding.

00:13:49.430 --> 00:13:51.300
Are you still filming this, you fuck?

00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:53.840
Morning of the third day,

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:55.958
hopefully Niki will wake
up and make us coffee.

00:13:55.958 --> 00:13:59.310
- [Niki] This has been a
very interesting experience.

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:03.820
- [Garrett] Look at it go.

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:05.739
- This is my favorite part of the RV.

00:14:05.739 --> 00:14:07.380
I definitely understand
the purpose that it serves

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:09.560
and I totally understand
why there are so many

00:14:09.560 --> 00:14:10.934
RVs in this park right now,

00:14:10.934 --> 00:14:12.720
but that being said, man,
it's been a challenge.

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:14.480
- This is probably the
most different living style

00:14:14.480 --> 00:14:17.840
we've done, it's all in all a small space,

00:14:17.840 --> 00:14:20.189
but pretty efficient.

00:14:20.189 --> 00:14:22.190
We really had everything
we needed to live.

00:14:22.190 --> 00:14:23.240
- It's a transformer.

00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:24.840
This feels like something you do

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:28.270
with people that you know
you can piss off to no end

00:14:28.270 --> 00:14:30.400
and have them still love
you at the end of the day.

00:14:30.400 --> 00:14:31.620
I don't know if we're there yet

00:14:31.620 --> 00:14:34.070
and I don't know if this was good for us.

00:14:34.070 --> 00:14:36.905
This whole thing rocks when
you walk back and forth.

00:14:36.905 --> 00:14:38.289
- This thing?

00:14:38.289 --> 00:14:39.529
- [Niki] Yeah, you giant.

00:14:39.529 --> 00:14:41.050
- [Garrett] I don't
think this RV brought us

00:14:41.050 --> 00:14:43.950
closer together, it almost
pushed us further apart.

00:14:43.950 --> 00:14:44.783
- [Niki] It's been a challenge.

00:14:44.783 --> 00:14:45.980
I don't know where we go from here.

00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:48.520
I think he and I are
really ready to be alone

00:14:48.520 --> 00:14:50.060
and to be apart from each other right now.

00:14:50.060 --> 00:14:51.710
- I just needed to know
that she's never gonna

00:14:51.710 --> 00:14:54.610
wake up for a sunrise, what
am I thinking? (laughs)

00:14:54.610 --> 00:14:56.143
the Grand Canyon is breathtaking.

00:14:56.143 --> 00:14:57.780
It's unbelievable.

00:14:57.780 --> 00:14:59.460
Nothing does it justice
except for going there

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:01.780
and standing on the edge
and being like, oh my god.

00:15:01.780 --> 00:15:02.989
You gotta do it, at least once.

00:15:02.989 --> 00:15:04.231
You don't have to.

00:15:04.231 --> 00:15:05.759
Live your life however you want.

00:15:05.759 --> 00:15:06.940
- [Niki] This experience
has been very beautiful.

00:15:06.940 --> 00:15:07.970
We're seeing a part of the country

00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:09.130
that I've never seen before.

00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:10.640
The Grand Canyon's unbelievable,

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:12.230
driving through it's been really fun.

00:15:12.230 --> 00:15:15.190
- That said, I wanna get back to my house.

00:15:16.170 --> 00:15:17.487
So badly.

00:15:17.487 --> 00:15:18.553
- [Niki] Bye.

00:15:18.553 --> 00:15:19.871
- Bye RV.

00:15:19.871 --> 00:15:21.120
- [Niki] Next week

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:23.157
- [Garrett] On Home Buddies.

00:15:23.157 --> 00:15:25.550
- Arcosanti, what is it?

00:15:25.550 --> 00:15:28.200
It's almost as if we're
citizens of a new city.

00:15:28.200 --> 00:15:30.043
- [Lady] We'll have you work
in construction tomorrow.

00:15:30.043 --> 00:15:31.070
- Can I ask how much rent is?

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:32.380
- [Lady] $300 a month.

00:15:32.380 --> 00:15:33.460
- Wow.

00:15:33.460 --> 00:15:35.550
I don't think Niki's going to like this.

00:15:35.550 --> 00:15:37.820
- I'm getting some pod share vibes.

00:15:37.820 --> 00:15:39.240
- I'm really afraid that
at the end of three days

00:15:39.240 --> 00:15:40.890
I'm not gonna know what this was.

